<article class="env-lemma" id="04LU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04LU">Lemma <span data-tag="04LU">40.10.9</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid scheme over $S$. Assume $U = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ with $k$ a field. Assume $s, t$ are locally of finite type. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R$ is equidimensional, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\dim (R) = \dim _ r(R)$ for all $r \in R$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for any $r \in R$ we have $\text{trdeg}_{s(k)}(\kappa (r)) = \text{trdeg}_{t(k)}(\kappa (r))$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for any closed point $r \in R$ we have $\dim (R) = \dim (\mathcal{O}_{R, r})$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $r, r' \in R$. Then $\dim _ r(R) = \dim _{r'}(R)$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/04LP" data-tag="04LP">40.10.3</a> and Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02FY" data-tag="02FY">29.29.3</a>. By Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02FX" data-tag="02FX">29.29.1</a> we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim _ r(R) = \dim (\mathcal{O}_{R, r}) + \text{trdeg}_{s(k)}(\kappa (r)) = \dim (\mathcal{O}_{R, r}) + \text{trdeg}_{t(k)}(\kappa (r)).  \]
</div>
    <p>
       On the other hand, the dimension of $R$ (or any open subset of $R$) is the supremum of the dimensions of the local rings of $R$, see Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/02IZ" data-tag="02IZ">28.10.3</a>. Clearly this is maximal for closed points $r$ in which case $\text{trdeg}_ k(\kappa (r)) = 0$ (by the Hilbert Nullstellensatz, see Morphisms, Section <a href="/tag/01T9" data-tag="01T9">29.16</a>). Hence the lemma follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>